    "college": "Guru Nanak Institute of Technology",
    "description": "Welcome to Metamorph 2.0\nHey everyone! Welcome to Metamorph 2.0, an in-person hackathon hosted at the Guru Nanak Institute of Technology (GNIT) in Panihati.\n\nWe\u2019re bringing together students for a weekend of coding, hardware building, and hanging out with other creators. It doesn't matter if you're a seasoned developer, a hardware tinkerer, or if this is your very first hackathon\u2014there is a place for you here. We\u2019re covering all the essentials (food, Wi-Fi, workspace, and some cool swag), so you can just focus on building something awesome.\n\n\ud83c\udfc6 Prizes & Categories\nWe\u2019ve put together a total prize pool of \u20b91,00,000. Along with the main overall prizes, we have a dedicated Hardware Track for those who like building physical projects.\n\nWe also really want to encourage new faces in the tech community to build with us, so we have special prize categories reserved specifically for the Best Beginner Project and the Best All-Girls Team.\n\n\ud83d\udccc The Details\nWhen: September 12th - 13th, 2026\n\nWhere: Guru Nanak Institute of Technology (GNIT), Panihati\n\nFormat: 100% Offline / In-person\n\nCost: Completely Free\n\n\ud83e\udd1d Teams\nYou can participate with a team of up to 4 members, or just apply solo. If you're coming alone, don't worry\u2014we\u2019ll get you into our Discord server before the event so you can chat with other folks and form a team before the hacking even begins.\n\nApplications close on September 3, 2026. We're reviewing applications on a rolling basis, so drop your application through Devfolio and we hope to see you on campus!",
